f2b-manual-stats keeps per-address connection-attempt statistics for the
addresses banned in fail2ban's [manual] jail (pf table f2b-manual, anchor
f2b/manual).

pf counters live only in the kernel and are reset to zero on every OS reboot,
pf ruleset reload and fail2ban restart.  This tool samples the per-address
In/Block counters periodically, accumulates the deltas on disk and reports the
number of attempts per IP/CIDR over the last 90 days, so stale entries that no
longer generate traffic can be pruned from the jail manually.
